{"id": "EUVD-2026-80509", "enisaUuid": "fa56b7ae-8b46-3933-b4dd-77d72a3080a2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nLoongArch: KVM: Free init resources if kvm_init() fails\n\nkvm_loongarch_init() calls kvm_loongarch_env_init() to allocate the\nper-CPU kvm_context (vmcs) and kvm_loongarch_ops and to register the\nperf callbacks, and then calls kvm_init(). If kvm_init() fails its\nresult is returned directly, but since module_init() does not run the\nmodule_exit() stuff on failure, so kvm_loongarch_env_exit() is never\ncalled and those resources are leaked.\n\nSo call kvm_loongarch_env_exit() when kvm_init() fails, matching the\nteardown-on-failure pattern used by riscv_kvm_init().", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:54:42", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6bbbd7b719233645a5c120557a9ca1422e6b7a48", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6b78786ee7260d9818cf1d7a245b7a655ef83076", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3bf6f5e2e1007d38a5f35bd37e94ab645a0c40bc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f7a1064cce3b100b54780c68529176232d8eb01e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9g5j-xh66-prwm", "CVE-2026-89909"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0823b325-c594-3145-a1b0-193f9d01027f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2bd6ac68726131da32ace9717aa63ff68cf6605c <3bf6f5e2e1007d38a5f35bd37e94ab645a0c40bc"}, {"id": "1566c963-348a-369e-b5f9-20b9663ae5fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "744aeaf1-5f71-39f1-abac-47e345c213a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "761e6a37-75a4-353b-b0d6-e221b090bdfe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "7de0ef90-cd6b-3fef-9028-5353312c7c6b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7ef62265-c82d-3d13-8e00-1c2db9a96430", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2bd6ac68726131da32ace9717aa63ff68cf6605c <f7a1064cce3b100b54780c68529176232d8eb01e"}, {"id": "8d944aaf-205c-3f4c-b9e3-d91d349beebb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2bd6ac68726131da32ace9717aa63ff68cf6605c <6bbbd7b719233645a5c120557a9ca1422e6b7a48"}, {"id": "aa91ae84-42e4-32f6-92bb-6e325ff78aa7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "af0576c2-777d-3023-8729-2fc147b8f7e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2bd6ac68726131da32ace9717aa63ff68cf6605c <6b78786ee7260d9818cf1d7a245b7a655ef83076"}, {"id": "cb3be7c8-cda9-3547-b1d8-ba851e51f06f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0a1ad36d-0884-33d1-acc9-8a4aa5b4e180", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}